{
  "id": "proj-compost-bin-with-lid",
  "slug": "compost-bin-with-lid",
  "status": "published",
  "title": "Compost Bin with Lid",
  "summary": "A three-sided slatted bin with a hinged lid. Airflow gaps sized so it composts, not stinks.",
  "difficulty": "beginner",
  "estimatedHours": 4,
  "imageUrl": null,
  "currency": "USD",
  "steps": [
    "Pick a level, well-drained spot in part sun, close enough to the kitchen that you will actually use it, and clear it down to bare soil.",
    "Cut four 36 in posts from the 2x4s. Crosscut each picket in half to two 35 3/4 in slats, and cut the 1x4s into four 35 3/4 in lid-frame pieces.",
    "Build two side panels: lay two posts flat and parallel, then screw five slats across them with 1 5/8 in deck screws, starting 2 in up from the bottom and leaving a 1 in gap between slats (use a scrap as a spacer). Those gaps are what keep the pile aerobic.",
    "Stand the side panels up 36 in apart and screw five more slats across the back posts with the same 1 in gaps. Leave the front open so you can turn and dig out the pile.",
    "Flip the bin over, staple hardware cloth across the bottom, and fold the edges 2 in up the inside to keep rodents out. Wear gloves: cut mesh ends are sharp.",
    "Build the lid: screw the 1x4 frame together with 2 1/2 in screws, then screw six slats on top with 1/4 in gaps so rain is mostly shed but the pile can still breathe.",
    "Hinge the lid to the top back slat with the two strap hinges and screw the pull handle to the front edge.",
    "Set the bin on its spot and start filling: about three parts browns (dry leaves, cardboard) to one part greens (kitchen scraps, grass) by volume, kept as damp as a wrung-out sponge. Turn it through the open front every two weeks."
  ],
